 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Good that you' thinking about it. For most people, it's not that important. A fast processor is useful though, especially if you' doing multiple things at once. Then look at the ones that do basic architecture tests. A dual core with hyperthreading will usually beat a single core without it. Not really. architectural tests are expensive to run on slow systems, so they' only available on the faster ones. Good idea. They' usually show a demo that freezes on a slow machine, which is very dramatic and neatly hits key points.",
